ndTime + gap, endTime]\\n\\nAnd the event must fit within one of these slots.\\n\\nFor the prerequisite gap, the event can't start until max(prerequisite end times) + gap.\\n\\nLet me implement this using the interval approach.\\n\\nOne more thing - for the \\\"batch optimization,\\\" I want to be more strategic. Let me think about a multi-pass approach:\\n\\nPass 1: Schedule events that are most constrained (few rooms fit, preferred room, etc.)\\nPass 2: Schedule remaining events in the remaining slots\\n\\nThis prioritization ensures that flexible events don't take slots that constrained events need.\\n\\nOK, I think I have a solid plan. Let me implement it.\\n\\nActually, there's one more subtlety. For the constraint on when an event can start given its prerequisites: the event's start time must be >= max(prereq end times) + gap. And the prerequisites could be in different rooms. This is from rule 4.\\n\\nBut also, the gap for same-room events (rule 3) is separate. So if event C has prerequisite A (in Room 1) and we want to place C in Room 2, the prerequisite gap still applies (A.endTime + gap <= C.startTime), even though they're in different rooms.\\n\\nAnd if we place C in Room 1, then we need BOTH the same-room gap (from the previous event in Room 1) AND the prerequisite gap (from A), so the actual earliest start is max(same-room-earliest, prereq-earliest).\\n\\nOK, let me code this.\",\"signature\":\"c3b638ac-a753-4286-a8cd-b490bbfba4ef\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":948,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":27904,\"output_tokens\":0,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"822af966-4391-4e26-8d7e-c0d980c90291\",\"uuid\":\"7dc777f5-9350-4474-abe6-e229802d61c3\"}\n21\t{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"c3b638ac-a753-4286-a8cd-b490bbfba4ef\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"c